k pre-flop. Opponent checked, so no bet to call. Checking allows seeing the flop cheaply. Raising risks stack with no equity. Folding is suboptimal since checking is free.\n\nReason: With low, unconnected, unsuited cards, the optimal play is to check and wait for the flop. This minimizes investment while preserving pot control. Raising would be speculative and likely lose chips long-term. Checking also maintains fold equity if the opponent acts post-flop.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
